-- title:
--   Charged work of paired-label selection
-- statement:
--   Let $n,k\in\mathbb N$, $S\subseteq[n]\times\{0,1\}$, and $b$ a Boolean occupancy flag. The routine $\operatorname{selectPaired}(S,b,k)$ scans for the zero-indexed $k$th label whose membership in $S$ agrees with $b$, and may fail to find one. Here $W$ is the model’s `otherSteps` counter, summing fair-bit and nonoracle word-operation charges.
--   $$W(\operatorname{selectPaired}(S,b,k))\le2n(2n+3).$$
--   This budgets exchange selection even when $k$ is outside the available range.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/PhaseChainWork.lean#L175-L199

